@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1210 = private unnamed_addr constant [19 x i8] c"unquoted-type-alias", align 1
@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1211 = private unnamed_addr constant [915 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks if [PEP 613] explicit type aliases contain references to\0Asymbols that are not available at runtime.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AReferencing type-checking only symbols results in a `NameError` at runtime.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, TypeAlias\0A\0Aif TYPE_CHECKING:\0A    from foo import Foo\0AOptFoo: TypeAlias = Foo | None\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, TypeAlias\0A\0Aif TYPE_CHECKING:\0A    from foo import Foo\0AOptFoo: TypeAlias = \22Foo | None\22\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is currently always marked as unsafe, since runtime\0Atyping libraries may try to access/resolve the type alias in a way\0Athat we can't statically determine during analysis and relies on the\0Atype alias not containing any forward references.\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 613 \E2\80\93 Explicit Type Aliases](https://peps.python.org/pep-0613/)\0A\0A[PEP 613]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0613/\0A", align 1
