@anon.158f56963078a041553d42a6ce1813d5.1276 = private unnamed_addr constant [521 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of wildcard imports.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWildcard imports (e.g., `from module import *`) make it hard to determine\0Awhich symbols are available in the current namespace, and from which module\0Athey were imported. They're also discouraged by [PEP 8].\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom math import *\0A\0A\0Adef area(radius):\0A    return pi * radius**2\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom math import pi\0A\0A\0Adef area(radius):\0A    return pi * radius**2\0A```\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#imports\0A", align 1
